---
alwaysApply: true
---

Always use `pnpm` for package management:
- `pnpm install` (not npm/yarn/bun install)
- `pnpm run <script>` (not npm run/yarn/bun run)
- `pnpm exec` for local binaries and `pnpm dlx` for one-off packages (not npx/bunx)
- Run standalone TypeScript scripts with `tsx` (e.g. `pnpm exec tsx scripts/foo.ts`)
- Prefer `pnpm typecheck` over running `tsc` directly as it uses TypeScript Go and is faster
